    "insight_copy_section_xMkWci": {
      "type": "insight-copy-section",
      "name": "Insight Copy Section",
      "settings": {
        "large_headline": "Why We Like It: Practicality",
        "copy": "<p><strong>Feasibility</strong>: As a&nbsp;low-calorie diet, the FMD still includes 3 structured meals per day. This not only makes the dietsafer than water-only fasting&nbsp;(which has been known to increase&nbsp;the risk of hypoglycemia&nbsp;as well as&nbsp;certaininflammatory markers),&nbsp;but more importantly more tolerable.&nbsp;&nbsp;(Ezpeleta et al., Nutrition Reviews, 2024)&nbsp;</p><p>The fasting mimicking diet can be easily integrated into&nbsp;your daily life, and while&nbsp;of course a 5-day low-calorie diet is still challenging,&nbsp;it&nbsp;doesn’t&nbsp;require you to be&nbsp;in&nbsp;a medically&nbsp;supervised clinical retreat setting.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>More effective than other forms of caloric restriction:</strong>&nbsp;While certain less restrictive approaches like intermittent fasting, constant caloric&nbsp;restriction&nbsp;and time-&nbsp;restricted&nbsp;eating&nbsp;(e.g.&nbsp;eating during an 8-hour window)&nbsp;or&nbsp;alternate day fasting&nbsp;may be considered safer and more&nbsp;feasiblethan the&nbsp;FMD,&nbsp;these methods&nbsp;don’t&nbsp;demonstrate&nbsp;the&nbsp;significant improvements&nbsp;across a range of&nbsp;diseases&nbsp;like the FMD.&nbsp;No&nbsp;other periodic dietary protocol has been tested across cardiometabolic risk, glycemic control, autoimmune disease activity, chemotherapy response, and biological-age markers within a single body of randomized evidence. (Mediterranean-diet comparison:&nbsp;npj&nbsp;Metabolic Health and Disease, 2023)&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Easiest nutritional intervention:&nbsp;</strong>The FMD design is explicitly intended to work \"without requiring but while preferring improvements in the daily eating habits,\"&nbsp;(applied only ~3–4 times per year or monthly). In trials where participants otherwise continued their usual, unrestricted diet and only added periodic FMD cycles, the diet produced measurable improvements in body&nbsp;composition, cardiometabolic risk factors, glycemic&nbsp;control&nbsp;and biological-age markers. Benefits persisted for weeks after resuming normal eating and were driven by the FMD cycles themselves rather than any sustained change in daily eating habits. (Brandhorst et al., Nature Communications, 2024).&nbsp;In other words,&nbsp;the FMD is&nbsp;an ideal first line dietary intervention,&nbsp;even&nbsp;if you do nothing else&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
      }
    },
